Not bundled — downloaded by the user's device at runtime
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The app downloads the following directly from their upstream repositories on
the device; they are not committed here or packaged in the APK:
  - Eclipse Compiler for Java (ecj) 3.39.0 ............ EPL-2.0
  - Kotlin compiler-embeddable / stdlib / script-runtime 2.1.0 ... Apache-2.0
  - R8 / D8 8.9.35 ...................................... BSD-3-Clause
  - Gradle wrapper / distributions ...................... Apache-2.0
  - Android platform-34 ZIP (android.jar; code to download API 29-35
    variants exists but is never called) ................ Android SDK terms
  - Termux "openjdk-17" runtime, pinned to 17.0.19 (the pinned file
    returned 404 when checked on 2026-10-10; the pool now has 17.0.20)
    ..................................................... GPLv2 + Classpath Exception
  - Termux "aapt2" and "aapt" packages, latest version from the live
    index (currently 16.0.0.4-2) ........................ Apache-2.0
  - Termux library packages, resolved from the live Packages index, so
    the set and versions can change. Currently: libc++, zlib, libiconv,
    libjpeg-turbo, libandroid-shmem, libandroid-spawn, littlecms (MIT),
    alsa-plugins and its dependencies (alsa-lib, pulseaudio,
    libandroid-sysv-semaphore), libprotobuf, abseil-cpp, fmt, libexpat,
    libpng, libzopfli ................................... various (unverified)

Library dependencies resolved by Gradle (AndroidX, Jetpack Compose, Hilt/Dagger,
kotlinx-coroutines, kotlinx-serialization, OkHttp, apksig — Apache-2.0; XZ for
Java 1.10 — 0BSD) are listed in PROJECT-DOCUMENTATION.md.

